a4 { This move makes it clear that White is not doing well, as it bans permanently a queenside expansion based on b2-b4 due to ...axb3 destroying the pawn structure. } 16. Bg5 ( { The typical } 16. g4 $5 { weakens the f4-square but disrupts Black's play. However, in this position Black is coordinated enough after } Ne6 17. Nf3 Nd7 18. h4 Bc5 $15 { when he controls the dark squares. } ) 
Nfd7 17. Bg4 ( { White was also doing badly after } 17. Be3 Ne6 18. Nf3 f6 $15 { followed by ... Bc5, when Black slowly takes control over the game. } ) 
h5 18. Bxd7 Nxd7 $15 { It is true that Whites light-squared bishop can be a bad piece in this structure, as it is obstructed by the c4- and e4-pawns. However, giving up the pair of bishops will be costly as Black will find a way to open the position. } 
