 { Eduardo Iturrizaga Bonelli – Kiprian Berbatov, Pamplona 2011 Learning objective: This game illustrates White’s c4-c5 break against Black’s centre. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. c4 Bg7 4. g3 O-O 5. Bg2 d6 6. O-O Nbd7 7. Nc3 e5 8. e4 c6 { We have reached the position of interest. } 9. Be3 $5 { This is a relatively rare but perfectly logical continuation. } ( { Much more common is } 9. h3 exd4 10. Nxd4 Qb6 { in the style of Chapter 17. } ) 
